WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.066 --> 00:00:02.101
-The Trump presidency

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.303
officially ended today

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.804
as Joe Biden was inaugurated

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.540
as the 46th president
of the United States

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.141
and wow!

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:10.777
Alright.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.845
So that's what it feels like

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.779
when you're not
grinding your teeth.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:14.981
I'd forgotten.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.883
And I think -- yeah,

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.485
I can see colors again.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:21.287
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:25.759
[Tender tune plays]

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:27.126
You know, over the last
four years,

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.562
whenever I imagined myself
finally saying those words,

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.999
I pictured us surrounded
by a jubilant audience,

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.901
reveling in the
collective catharsis

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.936
of watching this wretched,
awful man

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.637
slink away
from the seat of power

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:41.874
like a drunk who got kicked
out of a bar at 3:00 am

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.643
for trying to steal
the free pretzels.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:47.213
[ Slurring ]
No, these are my home pretzels.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:50.550
I brought these pretzels
from my home.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.718
Instead, I'm alone
in an empty studio,

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.420
no pomp, no fanfare,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.457
no senior citizens bussed in
from Paramus,

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.892
who were told
they had tickets to Dr. Oz.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.461
The only celebration
we could manage was

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.364
Wally holding a single balloon
covered in Purell.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.834
Keep that party going, Wally.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.203
And the reason for that is,
even amid this moment

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:13.740
of collective relief,
the nation is still in the midst

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.574
of several
unprecedented calamities,

00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:18.511
none of which will magically
disappear anytime soon.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:21.080
It's a little like getting rid
of the last guy at a party.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.182
We spent four years yawning
and stretching and hinting

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:24.417
that he should get out

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.286
and, when he finally leaves,
it is a relief,

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.855
until you remember you still
have to clean up all his puke

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.291
and he like puked everywhere.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.493
Luckily, we had this guy
working at the inauguration.

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:42.034
♪♪

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:45.004
Sir, who are you
and why do you rule so much?

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.505
I knew they were taking
extra precautions

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:47.807
after the raid on the Capitol,

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.609
but, apparently, none are more
prepared than scarf man.

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:53.579
Beautiful old scarf
draped loosely around the neck,

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.116
one mask peeking out
of a second mask,

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.651
a pack of wet wipes that,
like many of you,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.053
I confused
for a pack of Oreo minis --

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.622
"Is that guy about to eat Oreos
close to the mic

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:06.525
in some kind
of inauguration ASMR?"

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.194 line:0%
Later in the day,
we got to see the Bidens

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.697 line:0%
enter the White House residence,
but, before they did,

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:11.697 line:0%
the White House itself went

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:12.698 line:0%
through a deep cleaning

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:13.932 line:0%
as soon as Trump left.

00:02:13.932 --> 00:02:15.101 line:14%
-There's a deep clean

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.803 line:8%
of the residence
because of COVID,

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.971 line:8%
which includes, you know,
vacuuming drapes,

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:22.574 line:8%
wiping baseboards,
cleaning chandeliers.

00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:24.777
-Scrubbing out Diet Coke rings,

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.779
pulling loose hair
out of the drains,

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.448
trying to get ketchup
off the Constitution.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.217
I know they're saying the deep
clean is because of COVID,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.785
but, I mean,
even without the pandemic,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.420
if I were moving in
after Trump anywhere,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.122
I'd want the place fumigated.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:38.391
The guy was glued to his TV,
barely left his bedroom,

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.392
and only ate fast food.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.392
That place probably looks like

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:42.428
a locker on "Storage Wars"

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.897
or a studio apartment
in a rent-controlled building,

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:47.366
after the tenant who's lived
there for 80 years dies --

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:50.069
just piles of old newspapers,
loose change,

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.338
and a collection
of weird ceramic pigs.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.673
[ As Trump ]
What do you think, Betsy,
should I concede?

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:58.010
Betsy has concerns about the
vote count in Georgia!

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.946
It's not in Trump's nature
to leave

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.181
on a graceful, dignified note.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.282
Instead, he left in shame

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.617
and disgrace,
the way he should have,

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.085
scampering out early
in the morning,

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.688
like a college sophomore
doing the walk of shame,

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.891
though he did give us
one final Trump trademark,

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.959
chopper-adjacent, Q &amp; shout.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.896
[Rotors whirring]
-This has been a great honor.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.698
The honor of a lifetime.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.132
-Now, that will never
have to endure

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:21.901
another one of these again,
can I just ask,

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.470
how long does it take
to start a helicopter?

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.273
Like wouldn't it have been
better to wait until he got in

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.607
before firing the thing up?

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:30.542
I don't know.
Past is past.

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:32.946
Trump, of course, couldn't even
muster the bare minimum level

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.380
of grace and self-assurance

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.582
to attend his successor's
inauguration,

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:39.318
but he did, apparently,
want his helicopter

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.920
to do one last farewell trip
around the Capitol.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.624
-They just flew over here,
over the Capitol,

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.525
where these preparations
are underway

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.862 line:15%
for Joe Biden's inauguration
at any moment now,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.163 line:15%
in the next few hours,
of course,

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:54.033 line:15%
the inauguration that the
president will not be attending,

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.035 line:14%
but, apparently, wanted to see.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.703
-He looked
upon our nation's capital

00:03:57.703 --> 00:04:01.140
the way past presidents looked
over hurricane damage.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.975
[ As Trump ]
Well, love me or hate me,

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:04.210
you have to agree --

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.411
I [bleep] the place up.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.812
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:08.881
Mel, are you looking?!

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.882
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.851
Mel! Mel!

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:15.121
She's --

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.223
He was too scared to go
to the inauguration,

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.758
but he wanted
to see it from afar.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.126
He treats the hallowed customs
of our democracy

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:22.295
like a five-year-old

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.130
watching a scary movie
through his fingers,

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:27.399
so he took a whirl around D.C.
on the taxpayer's dime.

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.268
One last no-joy ride.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:31.036
And, now, the Biden
administration will have

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.872
to reckon with a series
of simultaneous crises

00:04:33.872 --> 00:04:35.407
unprecedented in our lifetimes.

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:36.976
Just because Trump is gone

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.378
doesn't mean all the destruction
he wrought is gone as well.

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:42.180
In fact, it's very likely
to get worse in the near term

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.716
and the conditions that created
him will remain as well,

00:04:44.716 --> 00:04:46.652
unless they're scrubbed
from our institutions

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:48.387
and our system
and our public life.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.556
But I do think
a small step forward

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.291
was hearing
the incoming president,

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:53.993
on the eve of his inauguration,

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:58.031
acknowledge the very real
human toll of the pandemic.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:02.668
-To heal, we must remember.

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:07.306
It's hard sometimes to remember,

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.508
but that's how we heal.

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.143
-I have to say
I was very moved by that

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:13.746
because there's been
this weird collective erasure

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.381
of the toll of the pandemic

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.216
because of the willful
criminal neglect

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.250
of the Trump White House

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.019
and its allies
in the right-wing media,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:23.188
an insistence that it will all
go away, that everything's fine,

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:24.490
and that what you're seeing
and hearing

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.059
with your own eyes and ears
isn't actually happening.

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:29.695
And a small first step
towards fixing that

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:30.896
is acknowledging it.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:33.532
Anyway, very powerful,
and a welcome change.

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:36.135
Now, let's hear what the
outgoing president had to say.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.436
-Have a good life.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.071
We will see you soon.

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:40.472
-"Have a good life"?

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:42.175
That's not
a presidential farewell.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:44.810
That's what your high school
crush writes in your yearbook,

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.412
as a final twist of the knife.

00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:54.920
Although,
even weirder than that was

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:58.190
what Trump said right before,
hinting that he might possibly

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.292
try to make some sort
of political comeback,

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:01.426
if he's not disqualified

00:06:01.426 --> 00:06:03.162
after the Senate
impeachment trial.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:06.732
-So just a goodbye.

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:08.100
We love you.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.603
We will be back in some form.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.971
-"In some form"?
What does that mean?

00:06:12.971 --> 00:06:16.408
[ As Trump ]
Whenever you see a black
plastic bag stuck in a tree

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:19.378
or a vulture on the shoulder
of the highway,

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.013
pulling the guts
out of a dead raccoon,

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.215
that'll be me.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:24.917
Not the dog turd
you wipe off your shoe,

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.852
but the one that stays
stuck in the treads,

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:28.221
you need to dig out
with a stick,

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.156
never quite getting it all,

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:31.957
because part of me
will always be with you,

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:33.325
in some form.

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:35.928
So, Trump held a pathetic,
forgettable going-away party

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:38.797
about the size of the lunch rush
at Hale and Hearty.

00:06:38.797 --> 00:06:40.733
In fact, Trump's farewell
was snubbed

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:43.136
by virtually everyone,
from his own vice president

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.570
to Republicans in Congress.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.273
Trump was so desperate
for attendees at this thing

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:48.875
that those who were invited
could...

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:52.778
I worked at "SNL" for 12 years

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:53.980
and, when I go back
to see a show,

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.748
I can't even bring my wife.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.184
They even sent invitations
to people who turned on Trump

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:00.786
and left in disgrace,
like Omarosa; John Bolton;

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:02.922
and even Anthony Scaramucci,
who said...

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:12.330
Yeesh!
That is embarrassing.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.100
That's like when you get
an invite to someone's wedding,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.400
even though you
only met them once,

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.436
five years ago,
at a friend's barbecue.

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:20.506
Honey, do you remember, Doug,
the guy from the barbecue,

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:22.408
wouldn't stop trying
to sell us insurance?

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:25.344
No?
Okay, well, uh,

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:27.480
do you want to go
to his wedding?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.182
He's offering 17 plus-ones.

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:31.450
Then, of course,
there was the fact that,

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.252
in his final address
as president,

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.154
he signed off the way
you'd expect,

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:37.723
by rambling
stream-of-consciousness style,

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.992
like he was describing a dream
to a therapist.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:42.795
-People have no idea how hard
this family worked.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:45.131
We were not a regular
administration.

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:48.500
Our vets are happy.
Our people are happy.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.002
Our military is thrilled.

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:54.340
If you look at what happened
until February a year ago,

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.640
our numbers were at a level

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.476
that nobody had
ever seen before.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:08:00.579
And, now, the stock market
is actually substantially higher

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:05.651
than it was at its higher point
prior to the pandemic.

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:09.054
So it's really, you could say
we built it twice.

00:08:09.054 --> 00:08:11.190
Be careful. Very complex.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.424
Be careful.

00:08:12.424 --> 00:08:14.827
Remember us when you see
these things happening.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.395
Remember us.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:18.531
I'm looking at elements
of our economy

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:21.533
that are set to be
a rocket ship up.

00:08:21.533 --> 00:08:23.102
It's a rocket ship up.

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:25.671
We got the vaccine developed
in nine months,

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:29.241
instead of nine years,
or five years or ten years.

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:32.011
-Even in his last address
to the nation as president,

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:34.747
he sounds like a husband making
small talk with the doorman

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:37.182
while he waits for his wife
to come down to the lobby.

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:40.119
[ As Trump ]
So, yeah, my cousin got
his master's in four years.

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:43.489
Could've been nine,
five, 10 years.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.991
She should be down soon.

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:49.495
Man, this Met season's
off to a crazy start.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:51.564
Then, Trump finished his speech,
or whatever it was,

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:53.032
and, in a bizarre spectacle,

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:55.367
he waved goodbye
to the anemic crowd

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:57.503
to the same song
he ended his rallies with.

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.772
-♪ YMCA ♪

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:01.406
♪ It's fun to stay at the ♪

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:04.676
♪ YMCA ♪

00:09:04.676 --> 00:09:08.180
-Like Grandpa leaving 10 minutes
into the wedding reception.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.749
And then, finally, it all ended

00:09:09.749 --> 00:09:11.850
and we got to watch
Air Force One take off

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:14.019
with Trump onboard as president
one last time,

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:16.522
presumably setting a course
straight for the Sun,

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:18.524
where he would burst
into a thousand rays of light,

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.825
never to be seen again.
Either that,

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:21.694
or he was making a run for it.

00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:23.696
[ As Trump ]
How long can you
keep this baby in the air?

00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:27.098
I need it to last until after
they subpoena my tax returns.

00:09:27.098 --> 00:09:28.367
Look out the window, Mel!

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:29.502
Oh, she's not.

00:09:29.502 --> 00:09:30.636
She's out today.

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:34.306
[ Laughter ]

00:09:34.306 --> 00:09:36.308
And then, there was the
inauguration at the Capitol,

00:09:36.308 --> 00:09:38.377
the same site that,
just two weeks ago,

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:40.278
was the scene
of a violent insurrection

00:09:40.278 --> 00:09:41.647
incited by the president.

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:43.982
We were treated, on one hand,
to scenes of hope

00:09:43.982 --> 00:09:45.984
and solemn ritual,
like the inspiring moment

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:47.853
when Capitol Police Officer
Eugene Goodman,

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:49.755
who bravely led
a group of rioters

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:52.124
away from the Senate floor,
arrived at the ceremony.

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:53.526
And then, on the other hand,

00:09:53.526 --> 00:09:54.893
there was a moment
of shamelessness,

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:56.628
from Ted Cruz,
one of the seditionists

00:09:56.628 --> 00:09:57.963
who tried to subvert
the election,

00:09:57.963 --> 00:10:00.266
taking selfies at the same dais.

00:10:00.266 --> 00:10:03.068 line:8%
-Can I tell you
how astounding it is here,

00:10:03.068 --> 00:10:05.738 line:8%
to, you know, overlook
the west front of the Capitol,

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:09.441 line:8%
the exact spot where,
just two weeks ago,

00:10:09.441 --> 00:10:12.278 line:8%
rioters, violent supporters
of President Trump,

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:14.613 line:7%
were scaling the scaffolding

00:10:14.613 --> 00:10:16.582 line:8%
that has now been replaced
with bunting?

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:19.118 line:8%
It is remarkable, also,
to see so many of those

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:21.186 line:8%
who had backed the president
in this effort,

00:10:21.186 --> 00:10:22.420 line:7%
like Senator Ted Cruz,

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.623 line:8%
who, just a moment ago,
was snapping selfies.

00:10:24.623 --> 00:10:29.728 line:7%
♪♪

00:10:29.728 --> 00:10:32.832
-Who on God's green Earth
wants a selfie with Ted Cruz?

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:34.466
I mean, of course,
the main problem with Ted Cruz

00:10:34.466 --> 00:10:37.335
taking selfies
is that the self is Ted Cruz.

00:10:37.335 --> 00:10:38.904
Good luck finding a filter
that makes you look

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:41.540
less like a rockabilly muskrat
with a wet diaper.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.309
But, as gross as that was,

00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:45.710
there were also the genuine
signs of promise and hope,

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.880 line:0%
like, for example,
the sight of Bernie Sanders

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.715 line:0%
showing up in a giant coat
and mittens,

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:51.116 line:0%
with a bunch of papers
in his arms,

00:10:51.116 --> 00:10:54.153 line:0%
like a public defender
whose car stalled in the snow.

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:55.287 line:0%
[ As Sanders ]
I'm here now. I'm here.

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:56.355
You can stop talking
to my client.

00:10:56.355 --> 00:10:58.023
Thank you very much.

00:10:58.023 --> 00:11:00.058
Could someone mail this for me?

00:11:00.058 --> 00:11:01.993
Bulk is fine.

00:11:01.993 --> 00:11:03.662
Although the best Bernie
appearance was, of course,

00:11:03.662 --> 00:11:06.065
this picture of him sitting
in his chair by himself,

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:07.166
like he was at Foot Locker,

00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:08.367
waiting for the salesperson

00:11:08.367 --> 00:11:10.068
to bring him the next size up.

00:11:10.068 --> 00:11:12.138
Biden's first act as president
should be to replace

00:11:12.138 --> 00:11:14.973
every Confederate monument
in the country with this statue

00:11:14.973 --> 00:11:16.609
of Bernie Sanders.
The plaque can say...

00:11:19.811 --> 00:11:21.447
In fact, one of the best things
about the new era

00:11:21.447 --> 00:11:23.148
we entered today
is that Bernie will now be

00:11:23.148 --> 00:11:25.217
the chairman of the powerful
Senate Budget Committee,

00:11:25.217 --> 00:11:27.485
where he'll be able to fight
for, among other things,

00:11:27.485 --> 00:11:30.055
expanded direct payments,
unemployment insurance,

00:11:30.055 --> 00:11:33.091
a $15 minimum wage,
and canceling student debt.

00:11:33.091 --> 00:11:35.027
He'll be able to hold hearings
on Medicare for All

00:11:35.027 --> 00:11:36.195
and the Green New Deal.

00:11:36.195 --> 00:11:38.030
Hell, he could change
the price of coffee

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:39.398
in the Senate break room,
if he wanted to.

00:11:39.398 --> 00:11:41.433
[ As Sanders ]
Six bucks for a cup of coffee?

00:11:41.433 --> 00:11:42.534
That's insane.
From now on,

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:44.036
you bring your own beans
from home.

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:45.537
You grind them up
in a pencil sharpener.

00:11:45.537 --> 00:11:46.705
Meeting adjourned.

00:11:46.705 --> 00:11:48.274
And then came the fanfare

00:11:48.274 --> 00:11:50.209
and the ritual
of the inauguration itself,

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:52.077 line:0%
including performances
from megastars

00:11:52.077 --> 00:11:53.411 line:0%
J.Lo and Lady Gaga,

00:11:53.411 --> 00:11:55.480 line:0%
which was a nice change of pace
from the Trump era,

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.116 line:0%
when the only musical acts
who would associate

00:11:57.116 --> 00:11:59.084 line:0%
with the president were
Three Doors Down

00:11:59.084 --> 00:12:02.021 line:0%
and the kids who got
stiffed by Trump.

00:12:02.021 --> 00:12:03.121 line:0%
You remember that?

00:12:03.121 --> 00:12:04.590
When Trump refused to pay

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:07.292
a bunch of children
who sang at his rallies

00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:10.362
and they had to sue him
to get their money?

00:12:10.362 --> 00:12:12.398
Sadly, there won't be any room
in the history books for that,

00:12:12.398 --> 00:12:14.633
but I assure you,
here at "Late Night,"

00:12:14.633 --> 00:12:18.070
we! will! never! forget!

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.337
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.337 --> 00:12:21.407
Overall, the day was not short
on inspiration,

00:12:21.407 --> 00:12:24.076
with a benediction
from Reverend Silvester Beaman

00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:28.180
and an incredible inaugural poem
from 22-year-old Amanda Gorman,

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.248
but perhaps the most
stirring words were delivered

00:12:30.248 --> 00:12:31.784
by Senator Amy Klobuchar,

00:12:31.784 --> 00:12:33.285
to describe J.Lo's rendition

00:12:33.285 --> 00:12:34.652
of "America
the Beautiful."

00:12:34.652 --> 00:12:35.821
-Well, that was great.

00:12:35.821 --> 00:12:38.656
-That was my aunt's review
of "Mamma Mia!"

00:12:38.656 --> 00:12:39.925
"Wow, that was great.

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:42.928
I liked all the singing
and the dancing.

00:12:42.928 --> 00:12:44.229
Time to go home!"

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:46.131
And, of course,
we also witnessed

00:12:46.131 --> 00:12:47.732
some breathtaking scenes
of history,

00:12:47.732 --> 00:12:50.702 line:0%
chief among them, the scene
of Justice Sonia Sotomayor,

00:12:50.702 --> 00:12:52.604 line:0%
the first Latina to serve
on the Supreme Court,

00:12:52.604 --> 00:12:54.973 line:0%
swearing in Kamala Harris,
the first female,

00:12:54.973 --> 00:12:58.109 line:0%
the first Black, and the first
Asian American vice president.

00:12:58.109 --> 00:12:59.812
Then, of course,
came the catharsis

00:12:59.812 --> 00:13:01.947
of seeing a person
who is not Donald Trump

00:13:01.947 --> 00:13:03.682
become president
of the United States,

00:13:03.682 --> 00:13:06.351
when Joe Biden officially
took the oath of office.

00:13:06.351 --> 00:13:09.988 line:8%
-Please raise your right hand
and repeat after me.

00:13:09.988 --> 00:13:13.725 line:8%
"I, Joseph Robinette Biden Jr.,
do solemnly swear..."

00:13:13.725 --> 00:13:17.395 line:8%
-I, Joseph Robinette Biden Jr.,
do solemnly swear...

00:13:17.395 --> 00:13:19.097 line:8%
-"...that I will
faithfully execute..."

00:13:19.097 --> 00:13:21.300 line:8%
-"...that I
will faithfully execute..."

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.903 line:8%
-"...the office of President
of the United States..."

00:13:23.903 --> 00:13:26.138 line:8%
-"office of President of the
United States..."

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:28.640 line:8%
-"...and will,
to the best of my ability..."

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.142 line:8%
-"...and will, to the best
of my ability..."

00:13:30.142 --> 00:13:32.344 line:8%
-"...preserve, protect,
and defend..."

00:13:32.344 --> 00:13:34.513 line:8%
-"...preserve,
protect, and defend..."

00:13:34.513 --> 00:13:36.648 line:8%
-"...the Constitution
of the United States."

00:13:36.648 --> 00:13:38.383 line:8%
-"the Constitution of the
United States."

00:13:38.383 --> 00:13:39.384 line:7%
-So help you God?

00:13:39.384 --> 00:13:40.552 line:7%
-So help me God.

00:13:40.552 --> 00:13:41.753 line:8%
-Congratulations,
Mr. President.

00:13:41.753 --> 00:13:43.989 line:7%
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:13:43.989 --> 00:13:46.659
-Son of a gun. Wally, give
that balloon another squirt.

00:13:47.759 --> 00:13:49.061
[ Laughing ]
There we go.

00:13:49.061 --> 00:13:51.296
The only bummer was
that Biden didn't end the oath

00:13:51.296 --> 00:13:53.398
by swearing to preserve,
protect, and defend

00:13:53.398 --> 00:13:54.933
the Constitution
of the United States

00:13:54.933 --> 00:13:56.635
"and cut the malarkey,
so help me God.

00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:58.003
Come on, man!"

00:13:58.003 --> 00:13:59.738
Biden's swearing in
will also be remembered

00:13:59.738 --> 00:14:03.175
for having the biggest Bible
anyone has ever seen.

00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:06.111
Does that also have
every Amtrak schedule ever?

00:14:06.111 --> 00:14:07.979
Does it have the lesser
known gospels?

00:14:07.979 --> 00:14:09.481
[ As Biden ]
Yeah, this one has Keith.

00:14:09.481 --> 00:14:12.017
He doesn't add much, but he
spills the tea on Matthew.

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:13.552
[ Laughter ]
Guy was always late.

00:14:13.552 --> 00:14:16.121
[ Laughter ]
Then came Biden's speech,

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:18.957
his first address to a divided
nation as president.

00:14:18.957 --> 00:14:20.626
And see if you
can guess the theme.

00:14:20.626 --> 00:14:25.664
-It requires the most elusive
of all things in a democracy:

00:14:25.664 --> 00:14:27.566
unity.

00:14:27.566 --> 00:14:28.867
Unity.

00:14:28.867 --> 00:14:33.405
With unity, we can do great
things, important things.

00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:39.278
History, faith, and reason
show the way, the way of unity.

00:14:39.278 --> 00:14:42.914
Without unity,
there is no peace,

00:14:42.914 --> 00:14:44.549
only bitterness and fury.

00:14:44.549 --> 00:14:47.853
And unity is the path forward.

00:14:47.853 --> 00:14:50.522
-"But why won't the Democrats
talk about unity?!"

00:14:50.522 --> 00:14:52.824
You know, Republicans incited
an insurrection

00:14:52.824 --> 00:14:54.359
and then complained
that Democrats

00:14:54.359 --> 00:14:55.628
aren't trying
to unify the nation.

00:14:55.628 --> 00:14:57.529
Meanwhile, Biden talked
more about unity

00:14:57.529 --> 00:14:58.897
than a marriage counselor

00:14:58.897 --> 00:15:01.366
who only gets paid
if the couple stays together.

00:15:01.366 --> 00:15:03.869
[ As Biden ]
Ben, you need to validate
your wife's feelings more.

00:15:03.869 --> 00:15:05.737
And, Carol,
don't repress those emotions.

00:15:05.737 --> 00:15:07.472
Communicate.
Now, let's hash this out

00:15:07.472 --> 00:15:09.174
and grab a brisket
at Houlihan's.

00:15:09.174 --> 00:15:10.308
Like any president,

00:15:10.308 --> 00:15:12.311
Biden has his strengths
and weaknesses,

00:15:12.311 --> 00:15:13.946
but clearly, one strength is

00:15:13.946 --> 00:15:16.014
his ability
to give the nation a pep talk

00:15:16.014 --> 00:15:17.749
and, in many ways,
his inaugural address

00:15:17.749 --> 00:15:20.718
was basically the halftime
speech America needed.

00:15:20.718 --> 00:15:25.090
-At this hour, my friends,
democracy has prevailed.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.092
My whole soul was in it.

00:15:27.092 --> 00:15:32.631
Today, on this January day,
my whole soul is in this.

00:15:32.631 --> 00:15:34.666
We can join forces,

00:15:34.666 --> 00:15:37.468
stop the shouting,
and lower the temperature.

00:15:37.468 --> 00:15:40.205
And today
we mark the swearing in

00:15:40.205 --> 00:15:42.374
of the first woman
in American history

00:15:42.374 --> 00:15:43.975
elected to national office,

00:15:43.975 --> 00:15:46.678
[ Cheering and applause ]
Vice President Kamala Harris.

00:15:46.678 --> 00:15:49.281
Don't tell me
things can't change!

00:15:49.281 --> 00:15:51.950
And here we stand,

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:56.021
just days after a riotous mob
thought they could use violence

00:15:56.021 --> 00:15:58.490
to silence
the will of the people,

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:01.193
to stop the work
of our democracy,

00:16:01.193 --> 00:16:04.429
to drive us
from this sacred ground.

00:16:04.429 --> 00:16:06.497
It did not happen.

00:16:06.497 --> 00:16:08.333
It will never happen.

00:16:08.333 --> 00:16:13.038
Not today, not tomorrow,
not ever! Not ever.

00:16:13.038 --> 00:16:14.506
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:16:14.506 --> 00:16:15.640
-I mean, I don't know about you,

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:17.109
but I thought
that was pretty uplifting.

00:16:17.109 --> 00:16:18.710
Can we check in
on Bernie real quick

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:19.878
and get his reaction
to the speech?

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:21.513
Okay.
Alright, he's digging it.

00:16:21.513 --> 00:16:23.181
I know him.
He's digging it.

00:16:23.181 --> 00:16:24.850
Just hearing a president
talk honestly

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.185
and straightforwardly
about our challenges,

00:16:27.185 --> 00:16:28.553
promising to fight
for democracy,

00:16:28.553 --> 00:16:30.889
or saying phrases like
"my whole soul is in it,"

00:16:30.889 --> 00:16:34.159
was both calming and jarring
after four years of a president

00:16:34.159 --> 00:16:36.562
who, if he ever mentioned
his soul at all,

00:16:36.562 --> 00:16:38.863
did so in context of selling it.

00:16:38.863 --> 00:16:39.965
[ As Trump ]
Hello, is this the devil?

00:16:39.965 --> 00:16:41.500
How much can I get for the soul?

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.001
Ten bucks?
Forget it.

00:16:43.001 --> 00:16:46.671
Everybody's listened to the
soul call with the devil.

00:16:46.671 --> 00:16:49.007
It was a perfect call.

00:16:49.007 --> 00:16:50.442
I called the devil.

00:16:50.442 --> 00:16:52.678
I didn't sell the soul.

00:16:52.678 --> 00:16:54.178
I got an offer.
I said no.

00:16:54.178 --> 00:16:55.547
It was a perfect call.

00:16:55.547 --> 00:16:56.615
[ Laughter ]

00:16:56.615 --> 00:16:57.883
Biden also showed deference

00:16:57.883 --> 00:16:59.051
to previous presidents,

00:16:59.051 --> 00:17:00.619
including one
who couldn't be there.

00:17:00.619 --> 00:17:05.991
-I know the resilience of our
Constitution and the strength,

00:17:05.991 --> 00:17:08.393
the strength of our nation,

00:17:08.393 --> 00:17:10.862
as does President Carter,

00:17:10.862 --> 00:17:14.098
who I spoke with last night,
who cannot be with us today,

00:17:14.098 --> 00:17:17.836
but whom we salute
for his lifetime in service.

00:17:17.836 --> 00:17:18.971
-Everyone loves Jimmy Carter.

00:17:18.971 --> 00:17:20.739
I'm assuming Carter wasn't there

00:17:20.739 --> 00:17:22.207
because of COVID protocols,
although,

00:17:22.207 --> 00:17:23.541
he's such a good person,
he's probably

00:17:23.541 --> 00:17:25.610
with his Habitat for Humanity
friends,

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:27.612
building Trump a house
in Palm Springs.

00:17:27.612 --> 00:17:29.414
[ As Carter ]
It's not as nice
as the White House,

00:17:29.414 --> 00:17:32.183
but, if you fill with love,
it'll be more than enough.

00:17:32.183 --> 00:17:34.019
[ As Trump ]
Oh, love's going to be
a problem, Jimmy.

00:17:34.019 --> 00:17:35.687
[ Laughter ]
But now,

00:17:35.687 --> 00:17:38.323
the challenge for Biden
and for Democrats in Congress is

00:17:38.323 --> 00:17:40.092
to follow these words
with action.

00:17:40.092 --> 00:17:42.627
Biden began today
by announcing plans to sign

00:17:42.627 --> 00:17:45.163
a raft of executive orders
undoing some of Trump's

00:17:45.163 --> 00:17:46.865
most heinous
and destructive policies

00:17:46.865 --> 00:17:48.199
and Senate Democrats

00:17:48.199 --> 00:17:50.736
have unveiled a package
of democracy reforms,

00:17:50.736 --> 00:17:52.003 line:14%
which are huge first steps.

00:17:52.003 --> 00:17:53.972 line:15%
Biden and Democrats in Congress
can't shy away

00:17:53.972 --> 00:17:56.441 line:15%
from doing what's necessary
to fix both what Trump broke

00:17:56.441 --> 00:17:58.109
and what was broken before him.

00:17:58.109 --> 00:18:00.078
Trump has left
the nation in ruins

00:18:00.078 --> 00:18:01.546
and he'll leave
as the most disgraced,

00:18:01.546 --> 00:18:03.215
unpopular president in history.

00:18:03.215 --> 00:18:08.052
And, as for Trump, look, I know
today can't be easy for him,

00:18:08.052 --> 00:18:10.288
so I would like to read
a few lines of a verse

00:18:10.288 --> 00:18:14.493
that I know means a great deal
to former President Trump,

00:18:14.493 --> 00:18:18.296
in hopes that it will soothe him

00:18:18.296 --> 00:18:20.933
on this difficult day.

00:18:20.933 --> 00:18:22.701
"Young man,

00:18:22.701 --> 00:18:25.103
there's no need to feel down.

00:18:25.103 --> 00:18:26.738
I said, young man,

00:18:26.738 --> 00:18:29.307
pick yourself off the ground.

00:18:29.307 --> 00:18:31.310
I said, young man,

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:33.778
'cause you're in a new town,

00:18:33.778 --> 00:18:37.248
there's no need to be unhappy.

00:18:37.248 --> 00:18:38.850
It's fun to stay at the...

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:41.320
-♪ YMCA ♪

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:43.021
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:18:43.021 --> 00:18:46.591
♪♪

00:18:46.591 --> 00:18:48.326
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:18:48.326 --> 00:18:49.627
over two million meals a year

00:18:49.627 --> 00:18:52.063
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:18:52.063 --> 00:18:53.698
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:18:53.698 --> 00:18:55.767
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:18:55.767 --> 00:18:58.403
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:18:58.403 --> 00:19:00.071
Stay safe.
Wash your hands.

00:19:00.071 --> 00:19:01.840
Wear a mask.
We love you.

